WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.334 --> 00:00:02.920
I'm going to Vietnam, and I'm
bringing em' beer!

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:03.921
(All)
Yeah!

00:00:03.921 --> 00:00:06.006
♪♪

00:00:06.548 --> 00:00:08.091
♪♪
(Helicopter blades whirring)

00:00:08.091 --> 00:00:09.927
The Colonel:
Yo, I'd like to go over to
Vietnam

00:00:10.594 --> 00:00:14.973
and track down all the boys in
the neighborhood and just give
'em a beer.

00:00:14.973 --> 00:00:18.018
I'm gonna show them that this
country is still behind them.

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:20.437
Because I'm going to Vietnam,
and I'm bringing 'em beer!

00:00:20.729 --> 00:00:21.563
(All)
Yeah!

00:00:21.563 --> 00:00:22.189
Yeah!

00:00:22.189 --> 00:00:25.567
I was pretty blown away that
this was actually based on a
true story.

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:27.402
No chance you have a
ship heading to Vietnam?

00:00:27.778 --> 00:00:28.612
1700 hours.

00:00:28.904 --> 00:00:29.571
Tonight?

00:00:29.571 --> 00:00:34.910
It's the story of a guy in 1967
who, during wartime, brought
beer to his friends

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:35.661
in Vietnam.

00:00:35.661 --> 00:00:37.037
Peter Farrelly:
Which is ludicrous of course.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:38.121
Ta-da!

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:39.540
Chickie?

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.959
Tom Collins:
I can't believe you came all
this way just to bring me a beer.

00:00:41.959 --> 00:00:43.460
It's the dumbest thing I ever
heard of.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.420
I knew I had to play Chickie.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:45.754
Ha-ha.

00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:48.090
Zac Efron:
I love the complexities and the
emotions.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:50.467
Zac Efron:
I love story of people learning
and growing

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:51.885
and embodying that.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.303
You're gonna get yourself killed
over there.

00:00:53.303 --> 00:00:56.348
It's like you said, everyone's
doing something.

00:00:57.432 --> 00:00:58.517
I'm doing nothing.

00:00:58.517 --> 00:01:01.937
Zac Efron, I've never worked
with an actor who was more open.

00:01:01.937 --> 00:01:04.982
Peter Farrelly:
This is a very different Zac,
then I think people have ever seen.

00:01:04.982 --> 00:01:06.942
Peter Farrelly:
He's just going a blow a lot of
peoples minds.

00:01:06.942 --> 00:01:07.776
Rick Duggan:
Do you think this is funny?

00:01:07.776 --> 00:01:08.819
I'm not doing this for laughs,

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:11.780
I'm doing it for you, for all
you guys.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:13.448
Russell Crowe:
Zac brought everything he could,

00:01:13.448 --> 00:01:17.953
And gave everything he had for
the roll and that was fun to be
around and fun to be apart of.

00:01:17.953 --> 00:01:19.204
Arthur Coates:
What did you say your name was
again?

00:01:19.204 --> 00:01:19.955
(Camera-shutter)

00:01:19.955 --> 00:01:20.998
Chickie Donohue.

00:01:20.998 --> 00:01:21.915
Arthur Coates:
Chickie Donohue,

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:22.833
is drinking on me.

00:01:23.166 --> 00:01:23.834
Arthur Coates:
Whoa!

00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:24.960
♪♪

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:28.297
Russell Crowe plays a war
correspondent who,

00:01:28.297 --> 00:01:30.090
Peter Farrelly:
ultimately takes Chickie

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:32.634
Peter Farrelly:
under his wing and helps him
out, and leads him in the right 

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.469
direction so he doesn’t get
his head blown off.

00:01:34.886 --> 00:01:35.387
Don’t shoot!

00:01:35.387 --> 00:01:39.057
There’s kind of a personal
connection for me because my
grandfather

00:01:39.057 --> 00:01:41.143
Russell Crowe:
was in fact a war photographer

00:01:41.143 --> 00:01:42.728
Russell Crowe:
so it was a very personal thing
for me 

00:01:42.728 --> 00:01:44.604
Russell Crowe:
to take on a character that did
that sort of job.

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:47.899
Why do you guys just report the
bad stuff. That’s what we hear
back home.

00:01:48.317 --> 00:01:49.443
Chickie Donohue:
I mean doesn’t that hurt us?

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:50.986
The truth doesn't hurt us.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:52.696
It’s the lies.

00:01:52.696 --> 00:01:53.864
Zac Efron:
Russell's just the coolest.

00:01:53.864 --> 00:01:54.906
Zac Efron:
He’s a hero of mine.

00:01:54.906 --> 00:01:56.116
Zac Efron:
Huge hero of mine.

00:01:56.116 --> 00:02:00.078
I was amazed at some of the
details that he was obsessed
with.

00:02:00.078 --> 00:02:03.123
Zac Efron:
It was really fun to see his
dedication to it.

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:05.584
I learned a hell of a lot from
working with him.

00:02:05.584 --> 00:02:07.377
Arthur Coates:
Smuggling beer into a war zone,

00:02:08.003 --> 00:02:10.005
Arthur Coates:
that’s not the smartest thing
that I ever heard of.

00:02:10.339 --> 00:02:11.757
Certainly not the worse either.

00:02:11.757 --> 00:02:13.008
♪♪
(Explosion)

00:02:13.008 --> 00:02:14.843
Russell Crowe:
That set was one of the most fun
sets

00:02:14.843 --> 00:02:16.678
I’ve been on in many many a
years.

00:02:16.678 --> 00:02:18.889
Russell Crowe:
It’s very easy to work with
Peter.

00:02:18.889 --> 00:02:19.806
♪♪

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:21.141
Zac Efron:
Peter is one of the most
interesting 

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:21.892
Zac Efron:
directors I’ve ever worked with.

00:02:21.892 --> 00:02:24.978
He doesn’t specifically come at
you with rules.

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:26.313
Zac Efron:
He's never stuck in one thing.

00:02:26.313 --> 00:02:27.731
Peter Farrelly:
Boom boom boom, couple more.

00:02:27.731 --> 00:02:31.318
Andrew Muscato:
I can’t imagine a better group
of people to ultimately make this movie.

00:02:31.318 --> 00:02:35.781
Peter Farrelly came off the
success he had with Green Book
to write and direct this.

00:02:35.781 --> 00:02:38.283
Andrew Muscato:
Just watching all these
incredible actors

00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:42.579
telling the story with humanity
and emotion has been very
fulfilling and exciting.

00:02:42.871 --> 00:02:44.623
Peter Farrelly:
Background, Action!

00:02:44.956 --> 00:02:47.709
Russell Crowe:
This film has a really big heart
and I think

00:02:47.709 --> 00:02:49.211
Russell Crowe:
it’s a really positive
experience.

00:02:49.211 --> 00:02:50.170
I think people are gonna love
this movie.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:52.756
Hey Colonel, one more round!

00:02:52.756 --> 00:02:57.177
This really is a powerful,
powerful story and in some ways
its-its never been more relevant.

00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:59.721
Zac Efron:
But it’s so kind of carefully
crafted and

00:02:59.721 --> 00:03:02.474
Zac Efron:
well written that there’s
moments where you’re gonna be crying,

00:03:02.474 --> 00:03:04.601
Zac Efron:
there's moments where you’re
gonna be laughing your ass off

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:09.481
and hopefully just transported
into another time and place.

00:03:09.481 --> 00:03:11.650
(Artillery fire)

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:12.484
We’re halfway home!

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:13.819
Halfway?!

00:03:13.819 --> 00:03:14.945
We're in No Man’s Land!

00:03:15.487 --> 00:03:17.114
So? I’m okay with that.

00:03:17.114 --> 00:03:20.992
♪♪

